### 1. Current user without cookies — expect 401.
# @no-cookie-jar
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/auth/me

### 2. Get a CSRF token.
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/auth/csrf

> {%
    client.global.set("csrfToken", response.body.token);
%}

### 3. Login with an existing account — expect 204.
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{csrfToken}}

{
  "email": "nazar.registration.check01@example.com",
  "password": "TestPassword123!"
}

### 4. Current user — expect 200 with id, name and email only.
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/auth/me

### 5. Refresh the CSRF token after login.
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/auth/csrf

> {%
    client.global.set("csrfToken", response.body.token);
%}

### 6. Logout without CSRF — expect 403; session must remain valid.
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/auth/logout

### 7. Still authenticated after rejected logout — expect 200.
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/auth/me

### 8. Logout with CSRF — expect 204 and an expired JSESSIONID cookie.
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/auth/logout
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{csrfToken}}

### 9. Current user after logout — expect 401.
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/auth/me
